  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>I like using Forester to track references, and I'd even like to
treat it as a Zotero replacement. I'm unsure what features I might need.
</html:p>
    <html:p>Oooh it would be great to have an "add reference" template and/or
keybind. Even better if there could be the ability to add by URL and
have the data properly parsed into the Forester reference format</html:p>
    <html:p>Implemented in <html:code>forester-org.el</html:code> with three interactive commands:
<html:code>forester-capture-reference</html:code> (manual entry),
<html:code>forester-import-reference</html:code> (from URL: DOI, arXiv, or publisher page),
and <html:code>forester-import-bibtex</html:code> (from clipboard BibTeX). Supports
DOI content negotiation, arXiv API, and HTML meta tag extraction
(Highwire Press / OpenGraph). Reference trees are created in
<html:code>trees/public/refs/</html:code> with <![CDATA[\taxon{Reference}
\meta{layout}{wide}]]> and embedded BibTeX.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
